    {
      "id": "claim_342e6c9a478c4b84b8c491f7f9918e00",
      "statement": "PromptValue is an abstract base enabling format-agnostic routing: StringPromptValue wraps formatted strings and converts to messages by wrapping as HumanMessage; ChatPromptValue wraps message sequences and converts to string via get_buffer_string(). Both implement to_string() and to_messages() methods, allowing downstream components to accept either representation flexibly.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/prompt_values.py#L24-L105",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:abe75a7764c81f1187a26f7fd65c2010f03d4c6efa620208dc44f8aa6cc51a63:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cfa4bbe1ce4c4d9ab064c2b5d4fa2933",
      "statement": "The partial() method (in BasePromptTemplate) pre-fills variables by creating a new instance with updated input_variables and partial_variables, without mutating the original. Partial variable values can be callables that are invoked at format time, enabling lazy evaluation. This immutability pattern enables safe reuse and caching.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/prompts/base.py#L289-L305",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f0b70ef20f8e415ad500cfe89851200dd312776c275c46ce989b2e9e3fe75500:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_23dfd2785c8a4ebda840bf98f5e44bc6",
      "statement": "BasePromptTemplate validates at format/invoke time that all required input_variables are provided via _validate_input(). It generates helpful error messages listing expected variables and suggesting that missing variables be escaped with double braces if they should be literal. The 'stop' variable name is reserved and raises ValueError.",
