          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2707790d91e39e81fdae7a9b3c815158a1a72490098cc17cb666e3416a3818fb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_268a20c672434b25a9f69e2332ebe67e",
      "statement": "ChatPromptTemplate and PromptTemplate support the + operator for composition. When composing ChatPromptTemplate instances, messages concatenate and input_variables merge. When composing PromptTemplate instances, both must have the same template_format, and templates concatenate. Conflicting partial_variables raise ValueError. The + operator returns a new instance without mutating operands.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/prompts/prompt.py#L142-L184",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:48d6f7aadd76acbbe01e11ec5724decd61a2baf0857c6f81e0e5f87769a25c89:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_167a6d30d524411096044f31bf8dc9ba",
      "statement": "Prompts serialize via langchain_core.load using dumpd() and loads() (recommended modern API). The older save()/load_prompt_from_config() API is deprecated (since 1.2.21, removal 2.0.0). Serialization preserves template content, format, input_variables, partial_variables, and message structure. Selectors using external resources (e.g., SemanticSimilarityExampleSelector with vector stores) are not serializable.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/prompts/base.py#L381-L400",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dbb78384eeb0de806904d1744938d48a475849b57aa03993b03ebd04464b6baf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_61bbebb3a7c74c58a712cf43c9612742",
      "statement": "Jinja2 templates use SandboxedEnvironment to block dunder attribute access (__class__, __globals__, etc.), but sandboxing is best-effort, not foolproof. Regular method calls and attribute access are allowed. LangChain recommends avoiding Jinja2 templates from untrusted sources and preferring f-string or mustache formats for user-controlled inputs.",
